1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Recap from THE TIMES, San Mateo County, August 5, 1963, front page, https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149938233/florence-isabella-fleishhacker:
2 CONT
2 CONT Florence Isabella Gerstle, daughter of San Francisco pioneer Lewis Gerstle (1824-1902) and his wife Hannah Greenebaum (1838-1930). Married 1904 to San Francisco businessman and financier Mortimer Fleishhacker (1866-1953) at Violet
2 CONC  Terrace, the Gerstle summer home in San Rafael.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Fleishhacker, an accomplished painter, was a member of the San Francisco Community Music School and the San Francisco Museum of Art. She died August 4, 1963 while painting at her summer home in Woodside, San Mateo County. Bur
2 CONC ial was August 6th in the Fleischhacker Mausoleum at Home of Peace Cemetery in Colma County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Fleishhacker was survived by her two children, Eleanor and Mortimer Jr, and sister Alice Gerstle Levinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT https://www.wescover.com/creator/bella-gerstle-fleishhacker
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
