1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Edgar M. Kahn's Pioneer S.F. Stockbrokers:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sloss was born on July 13, 1823, in Untereisenheim, Ba­varia; but he spent the greater part of his busy life in California. He was the youngest of five children, two brothers and three sisters. At seventeen he came across the plai
2 CONC ns to California, and in 1849 he settled in Sacramento. In part­nership with Simon Greenewald and Lewis Gerstle, he estab­lished in 1857 the mercantile firm of Louis Sloss and Com­pany. The flood of 1862 in Sacramento destroyed th
2 CONC eir store, and Sloss moved to San Francico to embark on new business ventures. He became a mining broker and was elected a mem­ber of the San Francisco Stock and Exchange Board in 1866. He resigned in 1873. In 1868 the Alaska Comm
2 CONC ercial Com­pany was organized and its presidency occupied his time and energy. Louis Sloss is remembered as humble and modest; a foremost San Franciscan and a generous humanitarian. He died at his home in San Rafael on June 4, 190
2 CONC 2.  With his passing the community lost one of its outstanding Jews. He is buried in Home of Peace Cemetery in San Mateo County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to great-grandson Peter Sloss (Z"L), Louis "came to California in 1849 via Louisville, where he had an older brother who had come to the U.S. before him. There are still Slosses in Louisville."
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis was first president of the Alaska Commercial Company, formed on Jan. 1, 1868, running the company with Mark Gerstle (identified as Lewis Gerstle).  The business of the company was to harvest Pribilof seals in the South Berin
2 CONC g Sea. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Information from the article, "Nature into Capital," from shapingsf.org/ezine/ecology/natureframe.html  Further:  "The official family histories of the Sloss and Gerstle clans and all their collateral branches depict the founders
2 CONC  as paragons of vision and probity in business, devoted as husbands, fathers and community leaders in their personal lives. They built family compounds in city and country (Slosses and Gerstles maintained an expansive Victorian es
2 CONC tate overlooking San Rafael) where wives and children were given every advantage that Alaska could provide, far from the messy killing fields of the Pribilofs."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Sacramento, Sacramento, California - 1850
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-431330151-1-500026/louis-loew-sloss-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-9b9423039101ca2e9529650477a97f7e&mrid=55dacb5a39ade71d0f7484af4a7c45f4 MyHeritage 
2 CONC Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 30 2017, 0:30:36 UTC''
2 CONT
