1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Marin (California) Civic Center Library's Oral Histories collection contains a recording, made on Aug. 9, 1980,  in which Katherine reminisces  "about 1900 Larkspur and Marin where the Solomons, Gerstles, Lilie
2 CONC nthals (who had summer homes) were all well known early San Francisco Jewish families. Descriptions of Escalle, Hills Boat House, Violet Terrace (the Gerstle home in San Rafael), & the 1906 earthquake are discussed on this tape as
2 CONC  are her San Francisco life, schooling, 1912 trip abroad, her marriage and a brief history of the Lilienthal, Solomon and Gerstle families."  Her birthdate is given as Feb. 3, 1911, which needs to be investigated.  The site is loc
2 CONC ated at http://www.cagenweb.com/marin/mmohp-l.html 
2 CONT see also http://contentdm.marinlibrary.org/digital/collection/ohp/id/636
