1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oakland Tribune, 12 Jan 1928, p17
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Systematic Cruelty Charged By Wife'''
2 CONT
2 CONT San Francisco, Jan 12-A complaint for divorce charging “systematic cruelty” over a period of one year “designed to persecute and annoy her” is on file here today against Dr. Sidney R. Dannenbaum, filed by his wife, Mrs. Genevieve 
2 CONC Dannenbaum, prominent in San Francisco society.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Danennbaum charges that he was cold and indifferent toward her and belittled and annoyed her before her friends. She asks permission to resume her maiden name of Genevieve Mills. A property settlement was made out of court.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Dannenbaum is living at 1926 Jackson street, following their separation of six months ago. She is a niece of Susan Mills, founder of Mills College. The couple was married by Superior Judge Trout on August 21, 1921.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oakland Tribune, 14 Jan 1928, p13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mrs. G. Dannenbaum Wins Divorce Decree'''
2 CONT
2 CONT San Francisco, Jan. 14--Mrs. Genevieve Dannenbaum is posessed with an interlocutory decree of divorce today from her husband, Dr. Sidney Dannenbaum. Before Judge Walter Perry Johnson she recited a tale of her husband’s sullen and 
2 CONC morose disposition and of his request that she move to Burlingame, leaving him alone in San Francisco. Her maid, Paula Publicovic, corroborated this testimony. The couple were married in July 17, 1921 and separated August 16, 1926
2 CONC . Mrs. Dannnenbaum is a niece of Susan Mills, Founder of Mills college.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oakland Tribune, 18 Aug 1936, p. 18
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mark Gerstle Weds in Reno'''
2 CONT
2 CONT San Francisco, Aug 18--Mark L. Gerstle and his bride, the former Mrs. Genevieve Mills Bennett, of Long Island, N.Y., were honeymooning today following their wedding yesterday at Reno.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage of the couple united two prominent families, both well-known here. Gerstle, president of the General Metals Recovery Corporation and the Townsend Company, has been a widower for two years. Mrs. Bennett was recently divorc
2 CONC ed from her third husband, Benno Hart Jr. in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple will make their home here, with Bryon Bennett, Mrs. Bennett’s son by a former marriage. She was previously married to two other San Franciscans, Dr. Sidney Dannenbaum and Raine Bennett.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage yesterday came only a few months after the announcement that Gerstle’s engagement to Mrs. Annabelle Lee, widow of Don Lee, automobile dealer, had been broken.
