1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Note Frank Sperling received on 3/16/2015:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hello there Sorry to bother you but I am in the processing of researching for a possible forthcoming book regarding the diaries of Evelyn Shillington during WW2 in England. I don't know if you are aware but Eugenia sent a large nu
2 CONC mber of children's dresses for the bombed out families of England under the USA Aid program prior to their entry to the war. Evelyn Shillington was working for the Womens Voluntary Service and noticed a Christmas card from Eugenia
2 CONC  in one of the dresses she made and felt duty bound to thank her for the many dresses she had made. The story made the San Fransciso Chronicle in June 1940. Evelyn and Eugenia became pen friends until Eugeina's death in the 1950's
2 CONC . I was hoping that you might have a photograph of Eugenia and Arthur circa 1940 to use in the book or there might still be some of the letters which Evelyn and Eugenia sent to each other. Many thanks for your time and I hope to h
2 CONC ear from you soon. Best wishes Shaun Sewell, Northumberland UK
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
