2 NOTE "In the late 1860s, The Seligman family transitioned from merchandising to banking, setting up operations in New York, St. Louis, and Philadelphia as well as Frankfurt, Germany, London and Paris that gave European investors an opp
3 CONC ortunity to buy American government and railroad bonds. The firm's conservative policies allowed it to ride out the panic of 1873.[17] In the 1880s the firm provided financing for French efforts to build a canal in Panama as well 
3 CONC as the subsequent American endeavor. In the 1890s J.& W. Seligman & Co. Inc. underwrote the securities of newly formed trusts, participated in stock and bond issues in the railroad and steel and wire industries, and invested in Ru
3 CONC ssia and Peru, and in American in shipbuilding, bridges, bicycles, mining, and other enterprises. " https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_investment_banking_in_the_United_States#The_%22Yankee_houses%22 
