1 NOTE {geni:about_me} New York Times, October 10, 1901
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notices - Theodore Hellman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore Hellman, the Stock Exchange member of the brokerage house of Seligsberg & Co., died early yesterday morning at his home, 36 West Seventy-fifth Street He underwent an operation for cancer of the throat last May, and until 
2 CONC recently had been at his camp near Lake Saranac in the hope of recovery. He was fifty-eight years old and had been the board member of Seligsberg & Co. since 1885. Before that he was a partner in the New Orleans branch of J. & W. 
2 CONC Seligman & Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Munich, Bavaria, and was married to Miss Frances Seligman, daughter of Jacob Seligman. He leaves three children, Edgar A., George, and Mrs. George Beer. Edgar A. Hellman joined the Stock Exchange this year. Mr. Hell
2 CONC man was a member of the Harmonie, Lotos, and Luncheon Clubs, President of the Eden Musee, a collector of paintings and etchings, and was interested in a number of musical associations.
