1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "a rare book / art dealer. He wrote fiction and poetry, translated Heine, wrote a book about Heine's life" 
2 CONT > part of: 
2 CONT ''"I have clear memories as a child of my grandfather: a very affectionate older man with a beard, married to my step-grandmother Irene--, visiting him in their country home. He left me a number of small paintings and books, dedic
2 CONC ated to 'my dear granddaughter Daisy".   My guess is that he died when I was about 7. He had a number of professions: Author, officer in the First World War, rare book dealer, art dealer, and according to my grandmother, a gambler
2 CONC . I believe he actually wrote a screenplay.  He wrote a number of books : fiction, poems, translations of Heine and such. He has a book of remembrances about selling letters and art to J.P. Morgan and such (still available from Am
2 CONC azon, to my surprise) called '''Lanes of Memory, Alfred A, Knopf, 1927'' 'Wherein we meet with poets and warriors, collectors and educators, statesmen and gamblers, statesmen and anarchists…and find the the fascination of human li
2 CONC fe consists in it's variety' He includes conversation and comments made by himself and fellow attendees at a meeting with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emma_Goldman Emma Goldman], and what she said in return. Written in the fairl
2 CONC y fustian style of the times, it also includes a chapter on auction bridge. It also includes flattering anecdotes with comments made by other art dealers about his "eye". However, I am very proud to possess "Grandfather's fake Tin
2 CONC toretto".''
2 CONT
2 CONT "He also wrote ''an unpublished History of the Seligman Family'', and supplied a large amount of material to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Our_Crowd ''"Our Crowd"'' the history of the Seligmans] and other intertwined German-Jewis
2 CONC h banking families. His own history is largely unreadable, however, being quite short on frank and clearly drawn pictures of the family members he was talking about, but including speeches made by prominent relatives in toto. "
2 CONT
2 CONT "My grandmother said that she got an MA, and got some help editing from him with her thesis, but ever after that he referred to it "rather unkindly, as 'our MA' ".  I find almost no mention of his father, Theodore Hellman, but he 
2 CONC was a member of the New York Stock Exchange. Apparently his father died when he was 22." ~• Daisy Paradis
