1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 18 Dec 1947 SF Chronicle, p. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT =Businessman Dies at 50
2 CONT
2 CONT Leon Sloss Jr., Automobile Dealer=
2 CONT
2 CONT Leon Sloss Jr., San Francisco auto dealer and a member of a pioneer California family, died suddenly yesterday. He was 50.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Sloss, whose home is in Woodside, was spending the night at the home of his father-in-law, Mortimer Fleishhacker, 2419 Pacific avenue. He was found dead in his bedroom yesterday morning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family friends said he had been under a doctor’s care for heart trouble. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Sloss, son of Leon Sloss, pioneer California financier, was a Stanford graduate in the class of 1920. At the time of his death he was serving his second term as president of the Stanford Alumni Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served 14 years as vice president of the Anglo-California Bank. He resigned this position in 1939 to go into the auto business with J. L. Glikbarg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Sloss wedding to Eleanor Fleishhacker in 1925 was one of the big society events of the year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was active in Community Chest activities and a member of the Family Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Sloss is survived by his wife, Eleanor; three children, Leon III, Nancy, at present studying at Bryn Mawr, and Peter, studying in Vermont; his mother, Mrs. Leon Sloss Sr.; a brother Louis, and a sister, Mrs. Lloyd Ackerman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 4 p.m. today (Thursday) at the Emanu El Mausoleum Chapel, Home of Peace Cemetery.
