1 OCCU Attorney
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Lucius Levy Solomons was an attorney, orator, and writer, based in San Francisco; also an officer in B'nai B'rith and the Romanian Relief Society; he married Helen B. Frank in 1896. The collection contains genealo
2 CONC gies; articles; speeches; correspondence; bulletins; accounts; and documents about the Solomons family and members of the Seixas, Green, Frank, Franks, Sloss, Lilienthal, Dorfman, and Spitzler families from Rhode Island, New York,
2 CONC  Jamaica, and London. It also contains the 1896 marriage license of Lucius L. Solomons and Helen B. Frank, signed by Rabbi Jacob Voorsanger; Seixas Solomons' 1856 certificate as being a first lieutenant in the Nineteenth Division 
2 CONC of San Francisco's Committee of Vigilance; together with speeches and articles written by L.L. Solomons, many with handwritten notes, on the meaning of Judaism; the Jew in the Diaspora; anti-Semitism; Palestine; immigration; phila
2 CONC nthropy; Jewish character; fraternalism and brotherhood; spiritual nationality; political Zionism; assimilation; altruism; justice; the Jewish soul; and the prophetic idea in Judaism.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.magnes.org/wjhc/finding-s.htm
