1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grave: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/118591657
2 CONT
2 CONT Jewish businessmen in Horb
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugo Frank from Nordstetten moved his textile business to Horb in 1864 and a year later he built a prestigious premises in an excellent location.
2 CONT
2 CONT More businessmen followed with their families, so that from 1864 to 1890 the Jewish population increased from six to 101 members. For example, the Gideon family came from Mühlen and founded a soap factory in Horb; the banker Adolf
2 CONC  Esslinger came from Mühringen; Hermann Tannhauser, proprietor of a shoe-shop, came from Dettensee; Jakob and Lippmann Stern, clothing manufacturers, came from further away, from Niederstetten in Hohenlohe.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ehemalige-synagoge-rexingen.de/en/jewish-prayer-room/history-of-the-community
2 CONT
