1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Personal: References: Staatsarchiv in Hamburg, death certificate index info: St. U (3a), Nr. (198), Tag (23.1), Jahr (28) which leads to an order number 9831 (332-5).
2 CONT
2 CONT Work: Moved from Stuttgart to Hamburg before 1906 when he and Raphael Jabi (or Zebi) Hirsch Bachrach formed "Bachrach and Loeb" a company in the leather trading business. Also involved in the business was Benjamin, a relative of R
2 CONC aphael who was born in Budapest. Raphael's wife was named Gertrude and they lived around the corner from Loeb at Fernsicht 7. The company was closed by Nazi's in 1939. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References: Staatsarchiv in Hamburg, Business File: HRA 28 559 and HRA 43 104. Business Tax reference code 314-15_R 1938/0321 and R1938/0324.
2 CONT
