1 OCCU Insurance Executive
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Levison -- insurance executive
2 CONT By Stacy Finz,
2 CONT Chronicle Staff Writer
2 CONT Feb 24, 2006
2 CONT Robert M. Levison Jr., a prominent insurance businessman and leader in the Bay Area's Jewish community, died of cancer Monday at his Atherton home. He was 78.
2 CONT Like his grandfather and father, Mr. Levison worked in the insurance industry -- providing policies to national and international firms. His grandfather was president of Firemen's Fund from 1917 to 1937, and later served as chairm
2 CONC an. His father and two uncles founded the insurance brokerage firm of Levison Brothers, which Mr. Levison joined in 1949. Two years later, Mr. Levison and two partners took over the company. In 1970, Mr. Levison merged his company
2 CONC  with another firm, which was called Dinner Levison. Eventually, Dinner Levison was sold to Transamerica, where Mr. Levison worked until he retired in 1997.
2 CONT According to his family, Mr. Levison was highly committed to community service and served as a board member of the San Francisco Jewish Community Federation, the National Conference of Christians and Jews, Jewish Family Service Ag
2 CONC ency, Palo Alto Medical Research Foundation, the Resource Center for Women and Rhoda Goldman Plaza.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert Levison's focus, his steady commitment and his good business judgment made the entire Jewish Community Federation and its partner agencies, from Mount Zion Health Systems to the Stanford Hillel, stronger," said Phyllis Coo
2 CONC k, associate executive director of the San Francisco Jewish Community Federation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Levison was born in San Francisco to Robert M. Levison, Sr. and Gertrude Guggenheim Levison.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife of 56 years, Anne Lehmann Levison; sisters, Ruth Halperin of Atherton and Barbara Napolitano of Bethesda, Md.; sons, James and David, both of Atherton; daughters, Joan Levison of Mill Valley, Marta Levis
2 CONC on of Atherton; and nine grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial service will be held at Congregation Beth Am in Los Altos Hills on March 26 at 2 p.m. The family asks that any donations be made to Stanford Hillel, P.O. Box 20526, Stanford, CA 94309, or the League to Save Lake Tahoe, 
2 CONC 955 Emerald Bay Road, South Lake Tahoe, CA 96150.
2 CONT
