2 CONC ritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 30 2016, 5:35:40 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rhoda Haas Goldman was an American philanthropist in San Francisco, California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Goldman was one of three children born to Walter A. Haas and Elise Stern and an heiress to the Levi Strauss fortune. She is a graduate of the University of California at Berkeley. In 1946, she married Richard Goldman. In 1951, the
2 CONC  couple founded the Richard and Rhoda Goldman Fund, a foundation that has donated over $680 million to various organizations. She was a major supporter of environmental causes and San Francisco arts organizations and a co-founder 
2 CONC with her husband of the Goldman Environment Prize in 1990.
2 CONT
2 CONT She served as president of the San Francisco Symphony, chairwoman of San Francisco's Memorial to the Six Million Victims of the Holocaust, director of the Mount Zion Health System, president of the Mount Zion Hospital and Medical 
2 CONC Center, and president of Congregation Emanu-El, the city's largest reform Jewish synagogue.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had four children with her husband, Richard Goldman: John D. Goldman, Douglas E. Goldman, Susan R. Gelman, and Richard Goldman. Funeral services were held at Congregation Emanu-El in San Francisco.
