1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meyer_Robert_Guggenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT Meyer Robert Guggenheim (May 17, 1885 – November 16, 1959) (often recorded as M. Robert Guggenheim) was an American statesman and a member of the prominent Guggenheim family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in New York City, he was the son of Daniel Guggenheim (1856–1930), brother of Harry Frank Guggenheim, and nephew of Simon Guggenheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served with the United States Army during World War I. He was appointed United States Ambassador to Portugal, serving between 1953 and 1954.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Meyer Robert Guggenheim died in Washington, D.C. in 1959, aged 74, and was interred in Arlington National Cemetery in Arlington, Virginia.
