1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bernard Gimbel was Chairman of the Board of Gimbel Brothers, Inc., which operated a famous chain of department stores. The "Macy's -vs- Gimbel's" feuds of the 1940's were legendary amusements in New York City. The 
2 CONC last Gimbel's store closed in 1987.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Obituary from the New York Times:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard F. Gimbel Dies at 81; Led Chain of Stores 34 Years; MOVE HERE IN 1910 BEGAN AN EMPIRE Expanded Family Business to 54-Member Group With Sales Near $600-Million 
2 CONT
2 CONT September 30, 1966, Friday
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 1, 2691 words
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard F. Gimbel, the exuberant merchant who brought Gimbels to New York in 1910 and became one of the world's dominant retailers as he ruled over his family's expanding network of department stores, died early yesterday in his s
2 CONC uite at the Pierre Hotel. [ END OF FIRST PARAGRAPH ]
2 CONT
2 CONT available in full at:  http://select.nytimes.com/mem/archive/pdf?res=F10A11FA3C58117B93C2AA1782D85F428685F9
