1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heiress to the Gimbels Department Store fortune.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The New York Times on Mar. 20, 2016 The International Council of The Museum of Modern Art is saddened to learn of the passing of Hope Gimbel Solinger, who died peacefully at home on March 6, at age 101. A member of th
2 CONC e Council since 1975, Hope was a spirited and valued member. She and her beloved twin sister Caral Gimbel Lebworth were frequent and generous participants in Council activities and travels. Hope will be fondly remembered by her Co
2 CONC uncil friends from all over the world. Our deepest sympathies are extended to her daughters Faith Sommerfield and Lynn Stern, and to her grandchildren and great grandchildren. Agnes Gund, Chair Sharon Percy Rockefeller, President 
2 CONC Jo Carole Lauder, President Emerita The International Council of The Museum of Modern Art.
