1 NOTE {geni:about_me}                                         BOSTON POST                   TUESDAY                    NOVEMBER 13. 1900
2 CONT                                                                 CHARLES WEIL'S SUDDEN DEATH
2 CONT                                                                      Expires at Hotel Somerset
2 CONT                                                                            Early This Morning Death came without warning to Mr. Charles Weil, one of the wealthy residents of the Hotel Somerset, while in his apartments, at 1:30 o’c
2 CONC lock this morning.  Mr. Weil, who was 62 years old, is survived by a widow, two sons and three daughters.  He was connected with the Filene family and was widely known. He had been slightly indisposed for two or three days, but no
2 CONC  apprehension had been felt.  Early this morning, however, he was suddenly stricken, and died without regaining consciousness.  The funeral arrangements will be announced later.
