1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Jewish Chronicle    -     page 9                                                                             January 1, 1954     London, England, United Kingdom 
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. ALMA MORGENTHAU
2 CONT
2 CONT The death occurred in New York on Friday, at the age of 66, of Mrs. Alma Morgenthau; a leading patron of the arts, especially music, Writes our NEW York CORRESPONDENT.  She encouraged contemporary composers "by commissioning their
2 CONC  works, and in recent years she extended her interests musical development of Israel.  After a visit to that country, she founded an organization there to publish the works of contemporary Israeli composers. This year she helped t
2 CONC o organize the archaeological exhibition – “From the Land of the Bible," held in New York and other cities.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Morgenthau, whose two marriages ended in divorce, was the daughter of the late Henry Morgenthau, who served as Ambassador to Turkey, and sister of the former Secretary of the U.S.A. Treasury.
2 CONT
2 CONT **** Per obits in the US - Mrs. Morgenthau took back her maiden name after he 1st divorce, from Mr.  Maurice Wertheim.
