2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Morgenthau, former United States Ambassador to Turkey, and Mrs. Morgenthau of this city have announced the marriage of their daughter, Mrs. Ruth Morgenthau Naumburg, to John Knight of New York, which took pla
2 CONC ce here yesterday noon at the New York County Court House in the chambers of Supreme Court Justice Philip J. McCook, who officiated. 
2 CONT ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
2 CONT
2 CONT POUND RIDGE, N.Y., May 17 —Mrs. Ruth Morgenthau Knight, a daughter of the late Henry Morgenthau, former Ambassador to Turkey, and sister of the late Henry Morgenthau Jr., Secretary of the Treasury under President Franklin D. Roose
2 CONC velt, died today in a hospital in New Canaan. She was 77 years old and lived at Blue Herons, her estate here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Knight was noted for her work as founder of the Ruth M. Knight Summer Theater Workshop in Bedford Hills, in which youngsters were trained, as she put it, not so much to become actors but “to develop as human beings.”
2 CONT
2 CONT She was also a founding trustee and president emeritus of the Hiram Halle Memorial Library in Pound Ridge, a former director of Fountain House and founder of the Ruth M. Knight Counseling Service of the Man hattan School of Music.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Knight's first marriage, to George W. Naumburg, a banker, ended in divorce in 1937. The next year she was married to John Knight of New York, a business man, who died.
2 CONT
2 CONT
