1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alan David Matzger, MD Passed away peacefully, Feb. 5, 2006 Born June 14, 1932. Alan attended Lowell High School, Williams College and UC Medical School. He practiced general surgery at St. Luke's Hospital and was 
2 CONC medical director of the Haight Ashbury Clinic and Bayview Hunter's Point Methadone Clinic. Upon retiring, Alan devoted many years of service to the SF Opera as a curtain page, the SF Performing Arts Library and was an avid fan of 
2 CONC the SF Giants where he worked as a ticket seller. Alan is survived by his beloved daughter, Cynthia Matzger; and sister, Jane Kauffman of Phoenix, AZ; and numerous nieces, nephews, great-nieces, great-nephews, cousins and loving f
2 CONC riends. He was the son of the late Edward Matzger and Claire Matzger Lilienthal; and brother of the late Paul Matzger. Private Services will be held. Donations may be made to the SF Opera, the SF Performing Arts Library and Museum
2 CONC  or Coming Home Hospice, San Francisco. Published in San Francisco Chronicle on Feb. 7, 2006 - See more at: http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/sfgate/obituary.aspx?n=alan-david-matzger&pid=16642802#sthash.Ieguf4v2.dpuf
