1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Colonel Hecht's escape from the 1906 San Francisco fire was accomplished despite the lack of disability access.  See this excerpt from his son-in-law's memoir:
2 CONT
2 CONT It was a motley crowd of women and children, and particularly my father-in-law, who had had a stroke and was paralyzed on the right side. It was in the early days of the automobile, and in our party there were only two. We piled t
2 CONC he women and children and Mr. Hecht into the automobiles, and the rest of us walked down to Fisherman's Wharf. It was a sad sight, but most interesting as I look back on it. When we got down to the wharf it was low tide. All of us
2 CONC  were able to climb down the ladder into the launch, but we had to tie Mr. Hecht into a bundle and lower him with ropes. 
2 CONT https://oac.cdlib.org/view?docId=hb4j49n9wb;NAAN=13030&doc.view=content&chunk.id=div00001&toc.depth=1&brand=oac4&anchor.id=0
