1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT David / Davied / Davele, born "Davied ben Jacob" / "David ben Jacob", took the surname Felsenthal when Napoleon decreed on 20 Jul 1808 that all Jews with no fixed family surname take a surname.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of his birth has been suggested to range between 1770 and 1776.  
2 CONT
2 CONT David was the son of Jacob Isaac (Jacob ben Isaac) b. 1732 in Waldgrehweiler, Germany; d. 14 Sep 1801 in Rathskirchen, Germany and Lea Benjamin b. 1743; d. 29 Jan 1813 in Odenbach, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT David had two wives
2 CONT # Anna "Johanna" (Hanne Abraham) Grünebaum b. abt 1780 possibly in Reipoltskirchen, Germany; d. 13 Jann 1818 in Odenbach, Germany
2 CONT # Barbara Grünebaum b. 1795; d. unk
2 CONT
2 CONT With Anna "Johanna" (Hanne Abraham) Grünebaum, David had the following children
2 CONT # Benjamin Wolf (Wolf Jacob) Felsenthal 1799–1861
2 CONT # Rosina (Bayer) Felsenthal 1801–
2 CONT # Judith (Judel) "Yettele" Felsenthal 1804–
2 CONT # Marianne Felsenthal 1807–1807
2 CONT # Jacob (Jakob) A Felsenthal 1809–1886
2 CONT # Johannetta / Jeannette Felsenthal Felsenthal 1812–
2 CONT # Abraham Felsenthal 1815–1815
2 CONT # Emanuel Felsenthal 1817–1818
2 CONT
2 CONT With Barbara Grünebaum, David had the following children
2 CONT # Hermann Felsenthal 1819–1897
2 CONT # Helena (Lina, Helen) Felsenthal Eichman 1821–1904
2 CONT # Philipp Felsenthal 1822–1895
2 CONT # Esther Felsenthal 1824–
2 CONT # Johanna Felsenthal 1827
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
