2 CONT
2 CONT Tiny, handwritten card to her parents on their 25th wedding anniversary:
2 CONT "To my darling [/]s - with every wish for as much joy in the future as there has been in the past - and with many many more years spent together. If having me has contributed to your happiness during the past twenty-five years - m
2 CONC ay the successive years make you happy by seeing me become a little more worthy of you. 
2 CONT All my love - Dots
2 CONT Just to make you feel a little nearer - More love and if possible more best wishes - from your devoted Dots"
2 CONT From Rosenberg Family Papers, 1860-1977, Box 1, 1:11, Bancroft Library, UC Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.nytimes.com/1977/08/08/archives/deaths.html:
2 CONT BERMAN—Louise R. Of San Francisco and New York City. On August 5, 1977. Beloved wife of the late Lionel Berman, beloved mother of Thomas R. Bransten and grandmother, of Marc, Katherine and Jeremy Bransten. Deeply mourned by her si
2 CONC ster in‐law, Mrs. Hortense Socholitzky and family, and by her many friends. Burial will be private, but a memorial service will be held in the fall.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT https://www.conservapedia.com/Louise_Bransten
