1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.sfgate.com/news/article/John-Walton-Dinkelspiel-2978229.php
2 CONT
2 CONT John Walton Dinkelspiel, a prominent San Francisco lawyer and former mayor of Atherton, died in Portola Valley on Friday. He was 94.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dinkelspiel was born in San Francisco and was the grandson of Moses Dinkelspiel, who opened the Dinkelspiel Store in Vallecito, Calaveras County, in 1852.
2 CONT
2 CONT The store is a state historical landmark. The Dinkelspiel Store was extended to include a saddle shop and later functioned as a Wells Fargo & Co. Express Office.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family became prominent in commerce in San Francisco, and supported the Valley Road, a railroad built at the turn of the century, from Richmond through the Central Valley, as a competitor to the Southern Pacific.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dinkelspiel's father, Henry G.W. Dinkelspiel, was consul of Siam in San Francisco.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dinkelspiel graduated from Lowell High School and the University of California at Berkeley, then from Harvard Law School, in 1926. He was sworn in to the California Bar on his 21st birthday, while still attending college.
2 CONT
2 CONT After graduating from Harvard, he joined his father and brother in the San Francisco law firm of Dinkelspiel and Dinkelspiel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He continued as a member of the firm until his retirement and its dissolution in 1989.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1942, Mr. Dinkelspiel joined the U.S. Navy. He served as flag secretary to Admiral John Hoover. He was awarded a bronze star and retired as a commander.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the war he moved to Atherton, where he served as Atherton city judge from 1948 to 1953. He was elected to the Atherton city council in 1967 and served as a member for 14 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was mayor of Atherton from 1982 to 1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dinkelspiel was a leading figure in the Republican party in California, and a close friend of Richard Nixon. He was prominent in Nixon's U.S. Senate campaign against Democrat Helen Gahagan Douglas in 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also Northern California chairman of the 1952 Eisenhower-Nixon presidential campaign and Northern California co- chairman of the 1960 Nixon-Lodge effort.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, in 1964 he was one of several prominent Republicans who supported Democratic president Lyndon Johnson against Republican candidate Barry Goldwater.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dinkelspiel was active in many community agencies and served on the boards of the San Francisco Jewish Community Relations Council and Homewood Terrace.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife Clara of Portola Valley, and his daughter Jean Chaitin of San Francisco.
2 CONT
2 CONT No services will be held.  Stephen Schwartz
