1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/sfgate/name/jean-chaitin-obituary?id=17434592
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Chaitin, born 1932, a fifth-generation San Franciscan. Died Aug 19, 2014 after a year living gracefully with lung cancer. Predeceased by her best friend and beloved husband of 54 years, Neil Chaitin; loving mother of Kenneth 
2 CONC (Jeri), Katherine, & Anne Chaitin.
2 CONT Jean got her BA from Wellesley and MS from SF State. She valued art, education and giving to her community. A docent at SF's Fine Arts and then Asian Art Museums, Jean founded the Asian's Community Speakers Program. She also serve
2 CONC d as: Board member and past-president Society for Asian Art; Board member Museum Craft and Folk Art; volunteer Friends of SF Public Library. In 1982, Jean joined the Fine Arts Museum staff and from 1990-98 was Director of Adult Pu
2 CONC blic Programs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon retirement Jean became an avid hiker. With Neil, she continued to travel widely and share a love for classical music, art, history and lifelong learning. To everything she did, Jean brought her curiosity and wide-ranging know
2 CONC ledge. But it was her loyal friendship, keen intellect, and quick humor that leave the biggest gaps; we will miss her deeply.
2 CONT
2 CONT At her request no services will be held. Gifts in Jean's memory may be sent to SF Public Library or Golden Gate National Parks Conservancy..
