1 TITL Hon.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Charles John Frederick Winn ''' (1896-1968) 2nd son of the 2nd Baron St. Oswald..
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an officer in the 10th Hussars from 1914 to 1922, and ADC to the British Military Representative at Marshal Foch's HQ in 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as Lieutenant of the 10th Hussars in the Great War. 1917 -  was injured at the battle of Monchy-le-Preux and lost his right eye.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the period before the Second World War, he managed the Winn family estate at Nostell Priory, Yorkshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.thepeerage.com/p8053.htm#i80527
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hon. Charles John Frederick Winn''' 
2 CONT * Born on 6 October 1896.
2 CONT * Son of Rowland Winn, 2nd Baron Saint Oswald of Nostell and Mabel Susan Forbes.
2 CONT * Married, '''firstly''', Hon. Olive Cecilia Paget, daughter of Almeric Hugh Paget, 1st and last Baron Queenborough and Pauline Payne Whitney, on 16 July 1919.
2 CONT * He and Hon. Olive Cecilia Paget were divorced in 1925.
2 CONT * Married, '''secondly''', Katherine van Heukelom, daughter of Henry van Heukelom, in 1929 - divorced.
2 CONT * Married, '''thirdly''', Theodora Thorpe, daughter of Warren Thorpe, on 17 August 1938.
2 CONT * Died on 1 May 1968 at age 71.
2 CONT * F/O AAF, Lieutenant 10th –22, WW I 1914–17 (wounded), Aide-de-Camp to Br Mil Rep at Marshal Foch's HQ 1918,
2 CONT * F/O 616 Yorkshire Aux (F) Sqdn 1938, Squadron Leader 1943, with Br Air Commn Washington, USA Hus 1914.
2 CONT * Educated Eton and RMC Sandhurst.
2 CONT * Lived at Nostell Priory, Wakefield, Yorkshire, West Riding, England. '''Children of Hon. Charles John Frederick Winn and Hon. Olive Cecilia Paget'''
2 CONT * Pauline Katharine Winn b. 18 Jul 1920
2 CONT * Susan Mary Sheila Winn b. 27 Apr 1923, d. Apr 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Child of Hon. Charles John Frederick Winn and Katherine van Heukelom'''
2 CONT * Michael Peter Anthony Winn b. 12 Oct 1933<br/>
2 CONT <span><br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Medal Index Cards 
