1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Born in 1947, Rick Goldman relocated from California to the East Coast, ultimately settling in Washington, DC with his wife Susan and their children. He began a legal career in public service as an assistant Unite
2 CONC d States attorney and then transitioned to private practice as a litigator, always maintaining an interest in and a concern for his community. In particular, Rick considered inequality, poverty, and criminal justice to be pressing
2 CONC  societal issues, and he focused much of his philanthropic efforts in those areas. Throughout his life, he led by example, instilling in his children the values of generosity, kindness, and empathy, as well as a charitable spirit.
2 CONC  The foundation is a tribute to his life and legacy."
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard W. Goldman Family Foundation https://www.rwgff.org/who-we-are/
