1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Lasker_(businessman)
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker (May 15, 1912 – July 11, 1997) was an American businessman and Thoroughbred racehorse owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the three children of Flora Warner and her husband, Albert Davis Lasker (1880-1952), the owner of Lord & Thomas, a highly successful Chicago advertising agency, who was also the owner of the Chicago Cubs Major League
2 CONC  Baseball team.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker graduated from Yale University in 1933. He then joined his father's advertising agency where he worked until 1941. After his father got out of the business, Edward Lasker then moved to the West Coast of the United St
2 CONC ates where he became a film producer in Hollywood. In 1947, Lasker married actress Jane Greer with whom he had three children. Their sons Alex and Lawrence Lasker are screenwriters and producers.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1929, Edward Lasker became involved in Thoroughbred horse racing as an owner/breeder. After his marriage, his wife also became a race horse owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT At age forty, Edward Lasker went back to university to study for a law degree. After graduating in 1955 from the University of California in Los Angeles he began practising law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker was living in Los Angeles at the time of his death in 1997 at age eighty-five.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Lasker_%28businessman%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker (May 15, 1912 – July 11, 1997) was an American businessman and Thoroughbred racehorse owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the three children of Flora Warner and her husband, Albert Davis Lasker (1880-1952), the owner of Lord & Thomas, a highly successful Chicago advertising agency, who was also the owner of the Chicago Cubs Major League
2 CONC  Baseball team.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker graduated from Yale University in 1933. He then joined his father's advertising agency where he worked until 1942 when he joined the U.S. Navy and served in the Pacific. After the war (by which time his father had le
2 CONC ft the advertising business), Edward Lasker moved to the West Coast of the United States where he became a film producer in Hollywood. In 1947, Lasker married actress Jane Greer with whom he had three children. Their sons Alex and
2 CONC  Lawrence Lasker are screenwriters and producers. In 1963, Edward Lasker married Cynthia Stone Palmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1929, Edward Lasker became involved in Thoroughbred horse racing as an owner/breeder. After his marriage, his wife also became a race horse owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT At age forty, Edward Lasker went back to university to study for a law degree. After graduating in 1955 from the University of California in Los Angeles he began practising law. He served for many years on the boards of directors 
2 CONC of Phillip Morris, Inc. and Great Western Financial.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lasker was living in Los Angeles at the time of his death in 1997 at age eighty-five.
2 CONT
