1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I found Judith's tombstone in the Schwanfeld Jewish Cemetery.  The Hebrew inscription translates roughly: "This memorial stone shall tell future generations that buried under it lies the esteemed, righteous and mod
2 CONC est woman Jetle, wife of Schlomo Gattmann from Schwanfeld. A God-fearing woman, pure-hearted and innocent, the pride of her husband, whom she used to assist. "
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Jetle is preceded by the Hebrew letter MEM, which is the shortened form of title MARAT, meaning Mrs. On the transcription the title and the name read מ' יטלא (and apparently, for some this looks like Mitla).
2 CONT
2 CONT The lower part of the stone is mostly undecipherable, and I was unable to identify the date of death... - Heartfelt thanks to Yaron Zakay for assistance in interpreting the inscription. ~jb
