1 NAME Alice /Sussmann/
2 GIVN Alice
2 SURN Sussmann
2 _MARNM Arnstein
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 NOV 1884
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 AUG 1951
2 ADDR
3 CITY San Francisco
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''Earthquake Hastens Pretty Girl's Wedding.  Walter Arnstein and Miss Alice Sussman were married yesterday by Superior Judge Lawlor at his residence, 2120 Jackson street. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of the earthquake Miss Sussman had been in a hospital for three days in preparation for an operation for appendicitis. After the disaster came, however, the operation was deferred, and Arnstein, who was about to leave 
2 CONC for New York, induced Miss Sussman to wed at once and make the trip to the metropolis their honeymoon. A marriage license was immediately secured in Alameda county and the ceremony was performed by Judge Lawlor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Arnstein is the son of the New York banker. His bride is a daughter of Mr. Sussman of the San Francisco firm of Sussman & Wormser. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: San Francisco Bulletin, 25 April 1906, page 3. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also appeared as: Quake Hurried This Wedding, Oakland Tribune, 25 April 1906, page 7.  Retrieved from San Francisco 1906 Earthquake Marriage Project  by sfgenealogy.com
