1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David William Lowe, 69, and Sandra Ann Spurling Lowe, 66, died in a car accident while travelling through South Carolina on February 16, 2011. David was born in San Francisco, CA, the son of the late William Leon L
2 CONC owe and Margaret Sloss Lowe, and grew up in Woodside. He worked in university relations and development for Pacific University in Forest Grove, OR for 17 years, and served for many years on their Board of Trustees. David was also 
2 CONC Vice President of Development at Florida Atlantic University in Boca Raton, FL for 18 years. Following retirement in 2004, David and Sandy moved to Marrowstone Island, WA. Sandra was born in Long Beach, CA, daughter of the late Ed
2 CONC win Brooks Spurling and Charlotte Ann Farrell Spurling. Her school years were in San Rafael, CA. Sandra taught high school English in Oregon, and was an adjunct professor of business and professional writing at Florida Atlantic Un
2 CONC iversity. They are survived by two daughters, Lyndsay E. Lowe of Los Angeles, CA, Judi Baldwin and her husband, Rob of Columbia, MD; and son, Matt Lowe and his wife Rochelle of Hillsboro, OR; and their five Grandchildren. David is
2 CONC  also survived by his two sisters, Ellie Kinczel of Oakland, CA and Jean Lowe of Paso Robles, CA. Sandra is additionally survived by her brother, Steven Spurling of Petaluma, CA. Memorial services were held in Marrowstone Island, 
2 CONC Forest Grove and Boca Raton. Con-tributions may be made to Lowe-Spurling Endowed Scholarship at Pacific University, www.pacificu.edu. Published in San Francisco Chronicle on May 22, 2011 - See more at: http://www.legacy.com/obitua
