1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From https://www.thefreelibrary.com/Obituaries.-a092965350:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Leon Bazalgette Russell of McKenzie Bridge died Sept. 27 of age-related causes. He was 87.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell was born Jan. 15, 1915, in Frankfurt Am Oder, Germany, to Charles and Phillis Meltzer Russell. He married Dorothy McEvoy in Hollywood, Calif. They later divorced. He was married to Madeleine Haas until their divorce in 195
2 CONC 9. He married Virginia Chames in 1962. She died in 1980. Russell married Cathryn Leinbach in Eugene on Jan. 14, 1983.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to the United States in 1934 after finishing high school in France. Russell lived briefly in North Carolina before moving to Hollywood, where he worked as a scenario writer for MGM Studios.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to World War II, he worked for the Office of War Information. Russell served in the Merchant Marine during World War II. He lived in San Francisco after the war and worked for Trans World Airlines. Russell also worked in the
2 CONC  restaurant business. He moved from San Francisco to McKenzie Bridge in 1960.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell enjoyed hiking, bicycling and fly-fishing. His interests included tennis and he hosted the McKenzie River Invitational Tennis Tournament at his home for many years. Russell was an avid painter, and he enjoyed nature, which
2 CONC  was the subject of most of his artistic work. Russell wrote a column, "Fluff and Stuff," for McKenzie River Reflections for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife; two daughters, Alice Russell-Shapiro and Christine Russell, both of San Francisco; a son, Charles of London; two half-sisters, Avery Russell and Claire Schaffner; and seven grandchildren. A daughter, Ja
2 CONC ckie, and a stepdaughter, Cindy Beckham, died previously.
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial service will be held in early 2003. Musgrove Family Mortuary in Eugene is in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial contributions may be made to the McKenzie River Trust, the McKenzie River Clinic or to Greenhill Humane Society.
