1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to the 1880 census, Joseph,  was a liquor dealer, was living on 449 Pine street in Meadville with his 24 year old wife Minnie and 1 year old son Samuel. According to the 1910 census, Joseph and Minnie mov
2 CONC ed to Kansas City and were living with their 21 year old son, Arthur S. (born 1889). Joseph became a merchant.  http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=75867320
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Elmwood cemetery in Kansas City: http://www.elmwoodcem-kc.org/family_history/elmwoodce-n/pafg21.htm#41845, Joseph was born on 17 May 1849 in , , , Germany. He died on 28 Aug 1915 in Kansas City, Jackson, Missouri. fro
2 CONC m car accident injuries He was buried on 31 Aug 1915 in Kansas City, Jackson, Missouri, (Elmwood Cemetery - H/168). He married MINNA J. WEIL. JOSEPH was employed as in Grocer. At the time of his death he was retired from the groce
2 CONC ry business.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, it seems that Joseph had a son by the name of Joseph born on 6 Apr 1889 in Kansas City, Jackson, Missouri. He died on 25 Oct 1954 in Kansas City, Jackson, Missouri, buried on 27 Oct 1954 in Kansas City, Jackson, Missouri, (c
2 CONC remated). Joseph was employed as in Consultant.
