1 NOTE {geni:about_me} October 12, 1869 New York Herald -- Joseph Fatman This gentleman, prominent among our Jewish fellow citizens, died in this city last week, and was burried Sunday evening last. Mr. Fatman was a native of Germany, wh
2 CONC ere he was born about 1813. He immigrated to this country about thirty years ago, and began life in the humble calling of a pedlar in Lancaster, Pennsylvania. By his energy and industry he was enabled, two years later, to open a f
2 CONC actory in Philadelphia, which he continued in operation some six years, at which time he moved to New York and began business as a retail dealer in cigars. About the year 1861 his transactions were exclusively wholesale, his firm 
2 CONC having become one of the largest in the tobacco trade in this city, with extensive branches in New Orleans, Galveston, Bremen, and Liverpool. While engaged in amassing the large fortune he possessed, Mr. Fatman found time to perfo
2 CONC rm works of charity. He was one of the most active officers of the Mount Sinai Hospital, and was for a long time president of the Hebrew Benevolent Society and the Orphan Asylum. To these institutions he made large donations, amou
2 CONC nting in one instance to $10,000, and was unremitting in releaving [sic] the wants of his coreligionists, as well as of the poor general. To the Jews of the country in particular, and to all lovers of humanity, whether Christian o
2 CONC r Jew, the intelligence of Mr. Fatman's death will be heard with regret.   From http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=19191087&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-962037554/joseph-fatman-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 19 2019, 18:30:47 UTC'
2 CONC '
