1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Myer E. Jaffa was an agricultural chemist, professor of nutrition at the University of California, and first director of the California Bureau of Food and Drugs. He was an early advocate of pure food and drug laws 
2 CONC for human and domestic animal consumption, and was associated with the movement which resulted in passage of the federal food and drug laws. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Collection #: WJHC 1969.010 AR1,
2 CONT
2 CONT Judah Magnes Museum, Berkeley, CA
