1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Hahn, Joachim: Jüdisches Leben in Esslingen. Geschichte, Quellen und Dokumentation, page 371. Partial translation:
2 CONT >He was married to Fanny (Friederike), Lazarus, on June 15, 1802. She was born as the daughter of Isaac Lazarus and Sara b. Ochs (see p.287f.) On 2 or 10 April 1786 (place of birth unknown).
2 CONT Page 372:
2 CONT >We learn the further life of Fanni (Friederike) Eßlinger from the Esslinger family registers ":" Friederike Eßlinger (actually Löser), daughter of Is. Lazarus, has lived for many years, separated from her second husband, Löser fr
2 CONC om Crailsheim. Their daughter: Jette Eßlinger «. After some time, Friederike Eßlinger returned with her daughter Henriette back to Esslingen, but it is not known where she spent the evening of her life. In Esslingen she did not fi
2 CONC nd her last retirement.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.freunde-juedischer-kultur-esslingen.de/historie2.htm
2 CONT >Leopold Abraham [1776 Dettensee - 1817 Rottweil], who bore the family name Esslinger from 1812, married Fanny [Friederike] Lazarus [1786 - her death date and her tomb are unknown]. They came with two small sons to Esslingen, wher
2 CONC e they were still five daughters, four of them already dying in the childhood - all with a "nervous fever" - in 1810 the family moved to Rottweil.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Famliy record:'
2 CONT https://www2.landesarchiv-bw.de/ofs21/bild_zoom/zoom.php?bestand=5632&id=1172179&gewaehlteSeite=01_0000446720_0014_1-446720-14.jpg&screenbreite=1440&screenhoehe=900
