1 TITL Dr. med.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Google translation to English:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Weil, Emil (Dr. med.) Surgeon, gynecologist Born on 12.01.1880 married in Munich
2 CONT
2 CONT Died (cause of death unknown) on 04.05.1935 in München (01.July 5695)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Hermann Weil, Salesman and Henriette Weil, born Steinmeier
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Marriage on 05.04.1933 in München with Anna Weil, born Herzog, born on 23.12.1898 in Glasgow, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Child (s): Paul, born on 17.10.1910 in Munich
2 CONT
2 CONT Addresses in Munich: Ottostraße 5 / I (since 01.01.1910) Hohenzollernplatz 11 a (since 03.02.1934) Platenstraße 1 / I (since 02.05.1934)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Emil Weil received his license to practice in 1906 and practiced until October 18, 1933 in Ottostrasse 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first marriage was with Edith, born January 12, 1910. Drey (born 28.07.1890 Munich) married. The marriage was divorced in 1912. Edith Weil married the ophthalmologist Dr. med. med. Eugen Selz, with him emigrated in 1939 via Lo
2 CONC ndon to the US, Edith Selz died on 17.11.1965 in Pasadena. The son Paul emigrated to France and later lived in California, he died on 15.08.2003 in Los Angeles. The second wife, Anna Weil, emigrated to Florence in the summer of 19
2 CONC 37.
2 CONT
2 CONT The grave stone of Emil Weil in the old Jewish cemetery on the Thalkirchner road is provided with graffiti from the Nazi era. So grave plates were marked, which should be melted down or otherwise used.
