1 NAME Leima Lehmann /Netter/
2 GIVN Leima Lehmann
2 SURN Netter
2 _MARNM Netter
2 NICK Lehman Leime Netter
1 NAME לימן //
2 GIVN לימן
2 SURN נטר
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1640
2 ADDR
3 CITY Duppigheim
3 STAE Alsace
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 JAN 1725
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rosheim
3 STAE Alsace
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU Leïma Netter, fermier du sel de la ville de Rosheim, avait acquis quelques masures dans le Wallgardt, fermier du sel de Rosheim
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://judaisme.sdv.fr/synagog/basrhin/r-z/rosheim/rosh-22.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/jeanbloch?lang=fr&pz=jean+camille&nz=bloch&ocz=0&p=lehmann+leime&n=netter
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-433027381-1-501607/leime-netter-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-6b29676ab3d0f88fc629df641d85d8b7&mrid=675ed41c10798ebee27ff03266201865 MyHeritage Famil
2 CONC y Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 16 2020, 1:13:18 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Netter, often spelled Nettre, Nedter, Nôder, is the name of a Jewish family from Rosheim, several members of which played an important role in Alsace in the 18th century.
2 CONT The first whose story has come down to us is Leïma Netter, born around 1645, lived in Duppigheim where he was perhaps born. The services he rendered to Baron de Montclar, Lieutenant General of the kingdom earned him his protection
2 CONC . This is how he was imposed on the Magistrate of Rosheim, who, willingly or unwillingly, had to welcome him within his walls. His son, Itzig, born around 1670, died in 1733, married around 1687 to Marion Heimendinger, was the rea
2 CONC l founder of the community of Rosheim. He built the synagogue in 1720, as well as the family home on the "New Jewish Street" which became "Rue Netter". He had two sons. The eldest Lippmann (1698-1772) married to Frumat Hertz of Ma
2 CONC nnheim, continued his father's action, faced with an always hostile magistrate, multiplying charitable and community institutions, hospices, hospitals for the elderly and sick, schools for all levels (yeshiva). The youngest, Lehma
2 CONC nn (1709-1792), was an entrepreneur " der Königlichen Fourrage ", banker, supplier of the armies, finally General Officer of the Jewish Nation in Alsace. He had married in 1729 Beyle, the daughter of Moyse David Oppenheimer, Court
2 CONC  Jew in Mannheim, in second marriage, Fraidel Elias, of Bingen.
2 CONT Thanks to their relations with the men in power, the Comte d'Argenson, the Duc de Choiseul, the General Officers of the Jewish Nation Moyse Blien, Aaron Mayer, Jacob Baruch Weyl, Lehmann Netter and Cerf Berr had succeeded in impro
2 CONC ving the political condition and social status of their co-religionists, to ensure them a certain intellectual advancement and relative security. Of all their actions, the most spectacular was the trip to Versailles by Aaron Mayer
2 CONC  and Lehmann Netter, during which they succeeded in obtaining the referral to the Parliament of Metz of the criminal case against Hirzel Lévy and his co-accused, condemned to death by the Sovereign Council of Alsace (1755). Mayer 
2 CONC Netter (1730-1805), son of Lehmann, experienced the Revolution and the ruin of the family. He tried to maintain the community during these difficult years. He had done extensive rabbinical studies. Detached from material things, h
2 CONC e did not succeed in regaining his ancestral fortune, which was left in assignats, but his conduct was exemplary in the face of the new ideas conveyed by the Revolution.
